create monorepo project with react typescript + .net

The monorepo is set up and both projects build successfully.

Structure
url-shortener/
├── frontend/                 # React + TypeScript (Vite)
│   └── src/App.tsx           # Calls /api/health
├── backend/
│   └── UrlShortener.Api/     # ASP.NET Core Web API (.NET 10)
├── package.json              # Root scripts + npm workspaces
├── UrlShortener.slnx         # .NET solution
├── .gitignore
└── README.md
What's included
Frontend — React 18 + TypeScript + Vite on port 5173, with a dev proxy for /api/* → backend.

Backend — ASP.NET Core minimal API on port 5104, with:

CORS for the Vite dev server
GET /api/health endpoint
OpenAPI in development
Commands
npm install          # install root + frontend deps
npm run dev          # run frontend + backend together
npm run build        # build both projects
Or run separately:

npm run dev:frontend   # http://localhost:5173
npm run dev:backend    # http://localhost:5104
The frontend shows API status by calling the backend health endpoint through the Vite proxy. You can extend from here with URL shortening logic on the .NET side and UI on the React side.